own and after seven nights used to live upon air. In this wise, passing seven hundred years they repaired bodily to heaven.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.719,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-13-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4013018","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"caf714a14d59d072e766959ce74eee7209b48ae8d63abc198ac36672c44f265c","compact":"b0bad579930e0fd47bd8604d83bc8172c8cc0ec79f6dc21271a91b1daf6abe34","nasal":"b0bad579930e0fd47bd8604d83bc8172c8cc0ec79f6dc21271a91b1daf6abe34"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-13-19","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":13,"verse":19,"english":"By virtue of their asceticism, this asylum is walled by trees and incapable of being conquered even by Indra, the celestials and the Asuras.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.708,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-13-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4013019","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"54dead1f2319c5994573982907ce5397763d51bed6247486c2c93bba4d52a51f","compact":"f36b1dc8e654b87ce40802f92b38038f197801b80841374361347dcbff13744b","nasal":"6f0368c8558e418d8c707e6f2fb5919a8acde5db6ab792ed4862be73eb10f8cf"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-13-20","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":13,"verse":20,"english":"Birds or other wild animals do not enter this asylum; whoever entereth this by mistake never returneth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.791,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-13-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4013020","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"519fc7afc97161d27888b1a64f52154778b80ab1cf20212450fbb0821d92ab04","compact":"d4446f940da9c365b77c2724a621ffe76b322a3ee7373d1b23ad4daca5c26a54","nasal":"5a32d987bcea4cf0dca2462e3bc253a653df0dc9a39787095113a8d1684391d7"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-13-21","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":13,"verse":21,"english":"There is audible, O Rāghava, the sound of the dressing of Apsarās, their sweet-winged accents and that of their music and drums; and herçin pervadeth the celestial fragrance.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-13-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4013021","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2e9fe271f75964509d1c0091438c7f44400ddf2630cd0d2d6999872d390a3104","compact":"796f0f1340e0c8b09c92522085c0fe9a4f815f5de617f8d2ede104cef8e447cd","nasal":"56f25ae20a5e30c77077152ccc410b563e0ff88893205e1e8106750f88de12db"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-13-22","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":13,"verse":22,"english":"Here burneth the fire Tretā; and the smoke and cloud sable like to the wings of a pigeon envelope the tops of the trees.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-13-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4013022","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1ebcad7c078bf669aeea00edf6575f8c0801ffc0f3cd9eacd41e6f74a26f936e","compact":"027b0e0bf8d6e7cc8e6155f685a7683a30f5de0054345e6822ba7ff2bb4af21a","nasal":"c81e0505c12d272d21922cb5f93574cc64c3015ca05ab587c5a6ddb07c563a98"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-13-23","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":13,"verse":23,"english":"Do you, O Rāghava, O virtuous-souled one, make obeisance to them along with your brother Lakṣmaṇa, with concentrated heart and folded palms.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.557,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-13-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4013023","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0190cd7c26b9cdc27ce7990c68e2bb44c581672e1d9113c8d